{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": ""}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Headings, Paragraphs and Styles in HTML"}, {"type": "position", "content": 4}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 1}, {"type": "level", "content": "B2.1"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you hear and use to talk about HTML tags"}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Understand information about common solutions to problems in spoken or written documents.   Describe concepts, principles, and important characteristics of hypertext preprocessor in spoken or written documents."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace.  Understands specific information in written texts about the different social and work contexts. "}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "enpe7n8le01ob04re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "make progress "}, {"type": "definition", "content": " to improve."}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb phrase)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Let\u00b4s just say I've made some good progress, though I think I will have finished this task by Monday."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n8le01ob04aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "the best thing since sliced bread "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the best innovation."}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(idiom)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Wow! This is the best thing since sliced bread!"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n8le01ob04aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "index "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to order."}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Search engines use them to index the websites that you're looking for, don't they?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n8le01ob04aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "blueprint"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a detailed plan."}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Remember that by this time next week, we will have presented a blueprint of the possible results to the managing board! "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n8le01ob04aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "managing board "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a group of people in charge of managing and taking decisions in a company."}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  Remember that by this time next week, we will have presented a blueprint of the possible results to the managing board!"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n8le01ob04aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "It's in the bag  "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "expression used when something will be a guaranteed success"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(idiom)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  It's in the bag! By then this will be the best designed website you have ever seen!"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n8le01ob04aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Look for more information on tags to design a web page with HTML "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Create a unique web design using the tags you have learned about. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write about HTML on your web site. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Share the web site with your partners."}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I talk about HTML tags for web design. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "I know tags used to style web pages. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "I write about HTML. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "I design great pages using HTML. "}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Future Perfect in Affirmative"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "We use the <strong>future perfect</strong> tense to talk about an action that will be completed before or around a specific time in the future."}, {"type": "text", "content": "The <b>future perfect</b> is normally used to express that: </br> <ul><li>Something will happen before another action takes place in the future</li> <li>Something will happen before a specific time in the future.</li></ul> </br> We often use the preposition <i>by</i> along with a time expression with this tense to indicate the time by which a certain action will take place or will finish. </br></br> To form the future perfect we use:</br></br>  <div align=\"center\">will/ going to + <b>have</b>+ <b>past participle</B></div></br>  Examples:</br> <i><b>By</b> the end of this session, you<b>'ll have understood</b> all about tags for paragraphs and headings in HTML.</br> Students <b>will have practiced</b> with different HTML editors <b>by</b> the end of the year.</i>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Let's just say I've made some good progress, though I think I will have finished this task by Monday."}, {"type": "example", "content": "We're launching it next week, and the researchers say that by next Friday it will already have had thousands of views. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Remember that by this time next week, we will have presented a blueprint of the possible results to the managing board!"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Tag Questions Negative - Affirmative"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "<b>Tag questions</b> are used in English to ask for confirmation or to encourage conversation."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Remember that <b>tag questions</b> are placed at the end of a sentence, and they are <i>negative</i> if the sentence is in its <i>affirmative form</i>, and <i>affirmative</i> if the sentence is <i>negative</i>. </br></br> Examples of <b>affirmative - negative tag questions</b>:</br> <i>This tag <b>defines</b> the title for your HTML document, <b>doesn't it</b>? </br> Students <b>can</b> practice with different editors, <b>can't they</b>?</i> </br></br>Examples of <b>negative - affirmative tag questions</b>:</br> <i>HTML <b>isn't</b> easy for new students, <b>is it</b>?</br> Tags <b>don't</b> help us to organize the code, <b>do they</b>?</i>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "You are telling me that you like the heading, aren't you? "}, {"type": "example", "content": "But, this heading doesn't look very powerful, does it?"}, {"type": "example", "content": " < h4 > ,< h5 > and < h6 > are too small for this, aren't they? "}, {"type": "example", "content": "This looks nice, doesn't it?"}], "type": "learning_points"}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "type": "welcome", "_data": [], "contents": [{}], "id": 0}, {"template_override": 1, "contents": [{"value": {"images": [{"time": "0", "image": "enpe7n8le01ob04re2img01.jpg", "id": 0, "text": "<strong>Jack:</strong> Hey Peter! How's our new website going? </br>\n<strong>Peter:</strong> Let's just say I've made some good progress, though I think I will have finished this task by Monday. I can show you if you want. </br>\n<strong>Jack:</strong> Wow! This is the best thing since sliced bread!</br>\n<strong>Peter:</strong> You are telling me that you like the heading, aren't you? </br><b>Jack</b>: I am. Headings are quite important, search engines use them to index the websites that you're looking for, don't they?  </br>\n<strong>Peter:</strong> That's why I'm a little concerned; we need to make sure they work, but we're launching it next Monday, and the researchers say that it will have had thousands of views by next weekend. </br>"}, {"time": "45000", "image": "enpe7n8le01ob04re2img02.jpg", "id": 1, "text": "<strong>Jack:</strong> But, this heading doesn't look very powerful, does it?</br>\n<strong>Peter:</strong>It does look powerful, but I think we are going to change the order. This one will be heading 1. h1 should be used for main headings, followed by h2 headings, then the less important ones with h3.  < h4 > ,< h5 > and < h6 > are too small for this, aren't they? </br>\n<strong>Jack:</strong> Yes, you're right. We need to include this information. Do you think this can be included in one paragraph? </br>\n<strong>Peter:</strong> Sure! All we have to do is open it with  < p > and close it with < /p >. Paragraph tags may include more than one sentence, pictures and, if you want, some other tags as well.</br>\n<strong>Jack:</strong> I see, but I would like this information to be inside a frame. I like the example I have here. This looks nice, doesn't it?</br>"}, {"time": "114000", "image": "enpe7n8le01ob04re2img03.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "<strong>Peter:</strong> Yes, it does.  We can use < br > if you want to start a new line without starting a new paragraph. We can put this inside the frame. </br>\n<strong>Jack:</strong> Good idea! But, what about the style? </br>\n<strong>Peter:</strong> it will be white and blue as we agreed. We can set the style by writing the following syntax: < tagname style=\"property:value;\"  ></br>\n<strong>Jack:</strong> Thank you for the information, Peter. I like how it looks so far. Remember that by this time next week, we will have presented a blueprint of the possible results to the managing board! </br>\n<strong>Peter:</strong> No worries. It's in the bag! By then this will be the best-designed website you have ever seen!</br>"}], "coverimg": "enpe7n8le01ob04re2img01.jpg", "audiosrc": "enpe7n8le01ob04re2aud01"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "type": "audio", "_data": [], "id": 1, "title": ""}], "exe